-- title:
--   Conductor lower bound for K₁(q^m)-fixed vectors in weight one
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ be a natural number, let $\psi$ be a Dirichlet character modulo $N$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$, and let $f$ be a cusp form of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(N)$ which is a primitive form with character $\psi$, in the sense that: its first $q$-expansion coefficient is $1$, the Hecke relations $a_{pn}+\psi(p)p^{k-1}a_{n/p}=a_pa_n$ hold for all primes $p\nmid N$ (with $k=1$), one has $a_{\ell n}=a_\ell a_n$ for all primes $\ell\mid N$, $f$ has nebentypus $\psi$, and for no proper divisor $M'$ of $N$ does the eigenpacket $\bigl(a_n(f),\psi(p)\bigr)$ occur in weight $1$ at level $M'$ (that is, there is no non-zero weight-one cusp form on $\Gamma_1(M')$ with some nebentypus satisfying the corresponding Hecke relations with eigenvalues $a_p(f)$ for all primes $p$ outside a finite set). Write $\varphi_f=\mathrm{weightOneLift}$ of $f$ at level $(N)\subset\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$: the function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ which on $g=\gamma h u$, with $\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, $u$ in the level-$(N)$ compact open subgroup, $h$ of trivial finite part and archimedean part in $\mathrm{GL}_2^+(\mathbb{R})$, takes the value $(f\mid_1 h_\infty)(i)\cdot\det(h_\infty)$, and $0$ where no such decomposition exists. Let $q$ be a prime and $m$ a natural number, and let $y$ be an element of the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$-translates of $\varphi_f$ such that: $y$ lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-linear span of the orbit of the distinguished generator $\varphi_f$ under $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$; $y$ is fixed by every element of $\mathrm{padicK1}\,q\,m$, the subgroup of those $x\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ which are the image of some $y_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}_q)$ whose lower-left entry lies in $(q^m)$ and whose lower-right entry is congruent to $1$ modulo $q^m$; and $y\neq 0$. Then the exponent of $q$ in the factorisation of $N$ is at most $m$.
--
--   This is the lower-bound half, in weight one, of Casselman's description of the conductor of the local representation generated by a primitive form: a non-zero vector of the local span at $q$ fixed by $K_1(q^m)$ forces $v_q(N)\le m$. It feeds into [`DihedralWeightOne.hasNewvectorConductor_adelicSpan_weightOneLift_factorization_of_isPrimitiveForm`](thm.html#DihedralWeightOne.hasNewvectorConductor_adelicSpan_weightOneLift_factorization_of_isPrimitiveForm), which records that the adelic span of the weight-one lift has newvector conductor exponent exactly $v_q(N)$ at $q$.
